Pharos is an infinitely tall concrete edifice visible anywhere on [[Færrin]]. One of its entrances is at 13 Bright Street in the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Aurideon/index|Aurideon]].

One can only see the building once they've already been introduced to it. It connects to disparate locations across the planet and on other planes. Navigation through the building is highly ritualistic, following the "Rule of Three."

The ground floor at 13 Bright Street is an office of the [[Org/Friends of Aut|Friends of Aut]]: reception desks beneath portraits of raimented figures of many faiths, and a black stone seal set into the concrete floor holding three blue gems. Past a stairway and an elevator is the threshold room, where the Friends keep a shelf of [[Phenomena/Voice Box|voice boxes]] and a black doorway, no door, that opens after three knocks into the [[Geography/Black and White/Plaza|Black and White]].

Coming back from the [[Geography/Black and White/index|Black and White]] is done the same way: three knocks on a black stone threshold set in a concrete wall return the traveler to the threshold room.

The [[People/Kellum Quinn|Kellum Quinn]] landscape *Second Meaning*, a view of the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Aurideon/index|Aurideon]] skyline, had the Pharos painted into it and then covered over with sky. The painting now belongs to [[Org/Prime Meridian/Rapid Connection|Rapid Connection]], and the Heart has stripped the outer paint so the tower shows beneath.
